span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> (<span class=\"fn\">b</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span>)</span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Induction principle for proving properties of `Int`-based ranges of the form `a<...b` by\nvarying the upper bound.\n\nIn the `base` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int` with\n`b ≤ a + 1`, the statement holds for the empty range `a<...b`.\n\nIn the `step` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int`, if the\nstatement holds for `a<...b`, it also holds for the larger range `a<...(b + 1)`.\n\nThe following is an example reproving `length_toList_roo`.\n\n```\nexample (a b : Int) : (a<...b).toList.length = (b - a - 1).toNat := by\n  induction a, b using Int.induct_roo_right\n  case base =>\n    simp only [Int.toList_roo_eq_nil, List.length_nil, *]; omega\n  case step a b hle ih =>\n    rw [Int.toList_roo_eq_append (by omega),\n      List.length_append, List.length_singleton, Int.add_sub_cancel, ih]\n    omega\n```","docLink":"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_roo_right","kind":"theorem","line":1273,"name":"Int.induct_roo_right","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L1273-L1307"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_roo_left\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">induct_roo_left</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">motive</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">base</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">b</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">step</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> (<span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span>) <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Induction principle for proving properties of `Int`-based ranges of the form `a<...b` by\nvarying the lower bound.\n\nIn the `base` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int` with\n`b ≤ a + 1`, the statement holds for the empty range `a<...b`.\n\nIn the `step` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int`, the\nstatement holds for nonempty ranges `a<...b` if it holds for the smaller range\n`(a + 1)<...b`.\n\nThe following is an example reproving `length_toList_roo`.\n\n```\nexample (a b : Int) : (a<...b).toList.length = (b - a - 1).toNat := by\n  induction a, b using Int.induct_roo_left\n  case base =>\n    simp only [Int.toList_roo_eq_nil, List.length_nil, Int.zero_eq_toNat_sub_iff, *]; omega\n  case step =>\n    simp only [Int.toList_roo_eq_cons, List.length_cons, *]; omega\n```","docLink":"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_roo_left","kind":"theorem","line":1240,"name":"Int.induct_roo_left","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L1240-L1271"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.getD_toArray_roo_eq_fallback\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">getD_toArray_roo_eq_fallback</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><s