IntLemmas.html#Int.toArray_toList_roo","kind":"theorem","line":933,"name":"Int.toArray_toList_roo","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L933-L936"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.toList_toArray_roo\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">toList_toArray_roo</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m</span>&lt;...<span class=\"fn\">n</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/Iterators.html#Std.Roo.toArray\">toArray</a></span>.<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array.toList\">toList</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m</span>&lt;...<span class=\"fn\">n</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/Iterators.html#Std.Roo.toList\">toList</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.toList_toArray_roo","kind":"theorem","line":928,"name":"Int.toList_toArray_roo","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L928-L931"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.toList_roo_eq_toList_rco\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">toList_roo_eq_toList_rco</span></a></span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>}</span></span>\n</span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">m</span>&lt;...<span class=\"fn\">n</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/Iterators.html#Std.Roo.toList\">toList</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">((<span class=\"fn\">m</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span>)...<span class=\"fn\">n</span>)</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/Iterators.html#Std.Rco.toList\">toList</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.toList_roo_eq_toList_rco","kind":"theorem","line":924,"name":"Int.toList_roo_eq_toList_rco","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L924-L926"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_rcc_right\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">induct_rcc_right</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">motive</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">base</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">b</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">step</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> (<span class=\"fn\">b</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span>)</span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Induction principle for proving properties of `Int`-based ranges of the form `a...=b` by\nvarying the upper bound.\n\nIn the `base` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int` with\n`b ≤ a`, the statement holds for the subsingleton range `a...=b`.\n\nIn the `step` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int`, if the\nstatement holds for `a...=b`, it also holds for the larger range `a...=(b + 1)`.\n\nThe following is an example reproving `length_toList_rcc`.\n\n```\nexample (a b : Int) : (a...=b).toList.length = (b + 1 - a).toNat := by\n  induction a, b using Int.induct_rcc_right\n  case base a b hge =>\n    by_cases h : b < a\n    · simp only [Int.toList_rcc_eq_nil, List.length_nil, *]\n      omega\n    · have : b = a := by omega\n      simp only [Int.toList_rcc_eq_singleton, List.length_singleton,\n        Int.sub_eq_iff_eq_add'.mpr rfl, Int.toNat_one, *]\n  case step a b hle ih =>\n    rw [Int.toList_rcc_succ_right_eq_append (by omega), List.length_append,\n      List.length_singleton, ih] <;> omega\n```","docLink":"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_rcc_right","kind":"theorem","line":884,"name":"Int.induct_rcc_right","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L884-L922"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_rcc_left\"><span class=\"name\">Int</span>.<span class=\"name\">induct_rcc_left</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">motive</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a> → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Prop</a></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">base</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">b</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LT.lt\">&lt;</a> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">step</span> : <span class=\"fn\">∀ (<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>), <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\">b</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> (<span class=\"fn\">a</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HAdd.hAdd\">+</a> <span class=\"fn\">1</span>) <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span> → <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></span></span></span>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">motive</span> <span class=\"fn\">a</span> <span class=\"fn\">b</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Induction principle for proving properties of `Int`-based ranges of the form `a...=b` by\nvarying the lower bound.\n\nIn the `base` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int` with\n`b < a`, the statement holds for the empty range `a...=b`.\n\nIn the `step` case, one proves that for any `a : Int` and `b : Int`, the\nstatement holds for nonempty ranges `a...b` if it holds for the smaller range\n`(a + 1)...=b`.\n\nThe following is an example reproving `length_toList_rcc`.\n\n```\nexample (a b : Int) : (a...=b).toList.length = (b + 1 - a).toNat := by\n  induction a, b using Int.induct_rcc_left\n  case base =>\n    simp only [Int.toList_rcc_eq_nil, List.length_nil, Int.zero_eq_toNat_sub_iff, *]; omega\n  case step =>\n    simp only [Int.toList_rcc_eq_cons, List.length_cons, *]; omega\n```","docLink":"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.induct_rcc_left","kind":"theorem","line":851,"name":"Int.induct_rcc_left","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.lean#L851-L882"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Range/Polymorphic/IntLemmas.html#Int.getD_toArray_rcc_eq_fallback\